2026-10-19T22:08:26.5379067Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 57210
2026-10-19T22:08:26.5379287Z   ISSUE_TITLE: tui: model picker omits configured local provider (ollama) models listed by CLI and API
2026-10-19T22:08:26.5384445Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Summary

The TUI model picker omits every model from a configured local provider (Ollama), even though the same models appear in `opencode models` (CLI) and in the API model registry. Users with a local Ollama provider configured cannot select any of its models from the TUI, which makes local providers effectively unusable from the TUI.

Reported by 0xacabos (host: 0xacabOS-DEV, user: badkuzushi).

## Environment

- opencode version: v0.0.0-detached-202610191902 (local build from upstream `dev`); symptom also observed on the installed 2.0.32 binary
- OS: Linux 0xacabOS-DEV 7.1.8+deb13-amd64 (Debian 13 base) x86_64
- Terminal: xterm-256color
- Shell: zsh
- Install/channel: detached (local build); repro attempts also made on the standard installed binary
- Active plugins: @cortexkit/opencode-antigravity-auth@latest, @dietrichgebert/ponytail, superpowers

## Reproduction

1. Configure an Ollama provider in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`:

   ```jsonc
   "ollama": {
     "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
     "name": "Ollama (local)",
     "options": {
       "baseURL": "http://localhost:11434/v1/"
     },
     "models": {
       "gemma4:12b": { "name": "Gemma 4 12B" }
       // ... further local models
     }
   }
   ```

2. Start `opencode` (TUI); the background service auto-starts.
3. Run `opencode models` — Ollama models are listed (19 entries with the Ollama server down; 25 with it up). The API model registry likewise contains them.
4. Open the TUI model picker (`/models` or `ctrl+x` then `m`).

## Expected Behavior

The picker lists the Ollama models (grouped under the provider), selectable like any other provider's models.

## Actual Behavior

No Ollama models appear in the picker. No error is shown; other providers (opencode-go, opencode-zen) list normally.

Consistent across: multiple fresh TUI processes, a full service restart, and two different binary builds (installed 2.0.32 and a fresh build from upstream `dev`). It is not explained by a stale TUI — reproduced in a TUI started after the binary swap and service restart.

Note: the model registry keeps the Ollama entries even when nothing is listening on `localhost:11434` (CLI still lists 19 models with the server down), so picker visibility is not a simple reachability filter either.

## Additional Context

- Source-reading leads from debugging the instance: the picker gets its data via `data.location.model.list(location.ref)` / `data.location.provider.list(location.ref)`; `useConnected()` / `hasConnectedProvider` in the TUI looked like the suspect gating, but reading `use-connected.tsx` suggested it only affects "connected" info display, not filtering — so the actual drop is elsewhere in that path.
- Related (possibly same root): with a default model pinned to an Ollama model and the local provider not routed, sessions fail immediately with `provider.no-route` ("Model unavailable: ollama/gemma4:latest").
- A rebuild from upstream `dev` fixed provider *registration* (models appear via CLI/API) but did not change picker behavior.
- Frequency: 100% of attempts over several hours of testing (2026-10-19).

